File: aruhan_memory_engine.support
Classification: INTERNAL — TRUSTED ENGINEERS ONLY
Module: ARUHAN Memory Engine (Y‑Prime Edition)
1. Overview
The Memory Engine is ARUHAN’s cognitive storage layer, responsible for:

short‑term memory

long‑term memory

episodic memory

semantic memory

memory decay

meta‑adjustment

It sits between the Dialogue Engine and the Knowledge Engine, providing structured memory signals to both.

The engine is deterministic, rule‑driven, and designed for stability under emotional fluctuation.

2. Memory Architecture
The Memory Engine contains four independent subsystems:

STM (Short‑Term Memory) — immediate conversational buffer

LTM (Long‑Term Memory) — emotionally weighted storage

EP (Episodic Memory) — event‑tagged emotional snapshots

SEM (Semantic Memory) — word‑frequency knowledge base

Each subsystem has:

its own decay rules

its own storage limits

its own weighting logic

This prevents memory overload and ensures predictable behavior.

3. Short‑Term Memory (STM)
STM stores the last 12 messages.

Characteristics:

fast turnover

high relevance

no emotional weighting

pruned by size only

Used for:

immediate context

coherence

short‑range topic tracking

STM is always safe to inspect and modify.

4. Long‑Term Memory (LTM)
LTM stores emotionally significant messages.

A message is stored if its emotional score exceeds 0.25:

Score formula:

|mood| × 0.4

stress × 0.3

energy × 0.1

LTM is used for:

emotional continuity

long‑term narrative patterns

meta‑learning

LTM is pruned by decay and size (max 500 entries).

5. Episodic Memory (EP)
EP stores emotion‑tagged events.

Each entry contains:

message

tag (pos / neg / neu)

mood

stress

energy

EP is used for:

emotional pattern recognition

narrative theme extraction

behavioral prediction

EP is pruned by decay and size (max 300 entries).

6. Semantic Memory (SEM)
SEM stores word frequencies across all interactions.

Characteristics:

dictionary‑like

no decay

grows indefinitely

used for concept weighting

SEM influences:

topic detection

knowledge inference

conversational grounding

Engineers may prune SEM manually if needed.

7. Decay System
Decay prevents memory overload.

Decay rates:

STM: 0.12

LTM: 0.005

EP: 0.01

SEM: none

Decay is applied by slicing off a percentage of the oldest entries.

Decay ensures:

stability

freshness

emotional relevance

8. Meta‑Adjustment System
Meta‑adjustment modifies:

drift

bias

coherence

Based on:

mood

stress

energy

Drift influences:

redirection behavior

memory weighting

Bias influences:

positivity/negativity tilt

Coherence influences:

memory stability

retrieval consistency

9. Rule Pipeline (Execution Order)
The Memory Engine executes in this exact order:

add to STM

add to LTM

add to EP

update SEM

apply decay

meta‑adjust

return snapshot

Changing the order will break memory consistency.

10. Debugging Entry Points
Safe to inspect:

STM

LTM count

EP count

SEM size

meta values

Safe to modify:

decay rates

storage limits

weighting formulas

Do NOT modify:

decay order

emotional scoring logic

episodic tagging rules

meta‑adjust formulas

11. Safe Modification Zones
Engineers may safely:

adjust STM size

adjust LTM emotional threshold

add new episodic tags

tune decay rates

expand semantic processing

Engineers must NOT:

remove memory subsystems

bypass decay

bypass meta‑adjustment

alter scoring formulas

modify pruning logic

12. Expansion Guidelines
When expanding memory capabilities:

keep subsystems independent

avoid circular dependencies

maintain deterministic behavior

test under emotional extremes

ensure compatibility with the System Orchestrator

13. Internal Philosophy
The Memory Engine is built on:

emotional weighting

deterministic decay

modular storage

narrative continuity

stability under drift

It is not meant to mimic human memory — it is designed for predictable emotional intelligence.

14. Notes for Trusted Engineers
Memory is the backbone of ARUHAN’s continuity.

All changes must be tested with emotional feedback loops.

Never modify memory while ARUHAN is running live.

Future integration with the Security AI will restrict access.
